        "modelAnswer": "<p><strong>Feature 1:</strong> Soldiers were ordered to rub whale oil into their feet daily, carry spare dry socks, and undergo regular officer foot inspections alongside raised wooden duckboards and pumps.</p><p><strong>Feature 2:</strong> Once body lice were linked to pyrexia (1918), troops were rotated through Divisional bathhouses and Foden steam delousing machines while ironing uniform seams.</p>",
        "pdfUrl": "",
        "mockUrl": "/units/edexcel_medicine/"
