        "modelAnswer": "<p><strong>Feature 1 (Executive Privy Council):</strong> One feature of Elizabethan government in 1558 was central executive rule through the Privy Council, which Elizabeth streamlined to 19 trusted nobles and administrators led by Principal Secretary Sir William Cecil to direct finance, defence, and daily royal policy.</p><p><strong>Feature 2 (Unpaid Local Shire Officials):</strong> A second feature was reliance on unpaid noble Lords Lieutenant and gentry Justices of the Peace in the shires, who raised local militia forces, enforced royal proclamations, and maintained law and order without a standing army or police force.</p>",
