        "modelAnswer": "<p><strong>Feature 1 (Disruption by Calais Fireships):</strong> One feature leading directly into Gravelines was Lord Howard and Drake sending eight unmanned burning fireships packed with pitch and gunpowder into Calais anchorage on the night of 7 August, panicking Spanish captains into cutting their anchors and breaking their defensive crescent formation.</p><p><strong>Feature 2 (Close-Range English Broadside Gunnery):</strong> A second feature on 8 August off Gravelines was agile English race-built galleons closing range to batter scattered Spanish warships with repeated broadsides while staying out of grappling reach, sinking or wrecking several vessels and driving Medina Sidonia north into the North Sea.</p>",
